Q: Data Exchange createExchange rejects published Revit Cloud Worksharing model source.fileId as malformed (EMEA) A: <p>The fileId and folderId are not the ID from Data Management API. They should be the ID value from the Data Exchange GraphQL API.</p>
<p>For the folderId, use the ID value from either of the queries below.</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>query GetProjectFolders ($projectId:ID!){
  project(projectId: $projectId) {
    id
    name
    folders {
      results {
        id
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>query GetFolderContent($folderId: ID!) {
  folder(folderId: $folderId) {
    id
    name
    folders {
      results {
        id
        name
        __typename
      }
    }
    items {
      ... on Items {
        results {
          id
          name
          extensionType
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>For the fileId, use the ID value of the items from the above folder query.</p>
